      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T19:07:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two pre-flight validation bugs before opening the USB device:\n1. **Malformed `-p` falls back to flashing `0BDA:5817` (lines 70–77)**: If the user explicitly specifies `-p` with a typo (e.g., `-p 0BDA-5817`), printing a warning and proceeding to flash default `0BDA:5817` risks flashing the wrong device. An unparseable explicit `-p` argument must fail immediately with `EXIT_FAILURE`.\n2. **Empty payload checked too late (lines 64–68)**: If the image is 0 bytes or contains only a 16-byte DFU suffix (`firmware.empty()` after `strip_dfu_suffix()`), `main()` still opens the device, enables download mode, detaches it into DFU mode (`0BDA:5800`), waits for re-enumeration, and only then fails inside `dfu_download()` — leaving the hardware in DFU mode. Please reject an empty payload right after `strip_dfu_suffix()` before touching USB.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "63a28113b244f691f4053b437b4f802da7ac6817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
