      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T19:07:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`rts5817_flash` currently cannot recover or flash an RTS5817 that is already in DFU mode (`0BDA:5800`, e.g., after an interrupted update):\n1. Without `-p`, it only looks for runtime PID `0x5817` and fails immediately when the chip is enumerated as `0BDA:5800`.\n2. Even with `-p 0BDA:5800`, `main()` unconditionally calls `enable_download()` — which sends `0x1A` (`GET_FW_STATUS`), a request the RTS5817 `STALL`s whenever it is already in DFU mode — followed by `dfu_detach()`, which resets a DFU-mode device *out* of DFU mode rather than entering it.\n\nPlease:\n- When `-p` is not specified and `0BDA:5817` is absent, also check for `0BDA:5800` (`kRts5817DfuPid`).\n- Whenever the opened device is already `0BDA:5800`, skip `enable_download()`, `dfu_detach()`, and `wait_for_device()`, and proceed straight to `dfu_download()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "63a28113b244f691f4053b437b4f802da7ac6817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
